  "limits": [
    "The initial positive used public anonymous Node-fetched bootstrap values solely as a diagnostic control in RAM; those values must not be shipped as a browser session.",
    "WEB JSON independently returns exact P1 infant notice, ID/status/embed and family-safe metadata for these three cases, so watch HTML is unnecessary for that observed gate. That gate is a product activation choice, not an external requirement.",
    "Replacing only the embedded visitor with a valid Music/WEB browser visitor or omitting it failed in the tested context. This does not prove impossibility of every pure-web method.",
    "The minimal recipe test also changed the visitor; its failure does not isolate a need for encryptedHostFlags or opaque extras.",
    "A single generic recipe was tested immediately, not for six-hour lifetime or all YouTube cohorts.",
    "The visitor-controls report summary counts its main player array and therefore excludes its positive controls; use recorded controls with the explicit frozen-order label correction above.",
    "First preflight marker-comparison error, initial HTTP400 body cancellation and overwritten observer labels are retained, not recast as provider results.",
    "The final HTTP400 JSON is readable but contains no responseContext or visitor. The last no-cookie embed GET is HTTP200 with MissingAllowOriginHeader.",
    "No signature/n transformation, CDN media request, song playback, phone/background or screen-off success is claimed."
